  "keyFindings": {
    "underfilledExplanation": "At 100k rows with ef_search=40 and iterative_scan=off, 66% (33/50) of queries returned fewer than 3 rows, causing recall@3 of 0.7%. This proves the prior 3.3% anomaly was caused by filtered vector search exhausting ef_search candidates before finding matching domain/topic rows.",
    "btreeEfficiency": "At 10k rows, exact scan with a composite B-Tree index on (domain, topic) achieves 2.14ms p50 with 100% recall and a tiny 88 kB index, outperforming global HNSW (3.48ms p50, 39 MB index, 14.6s build time).",
    "iterativeScanTradeoff": "Setting hnsw.iterative_scan=relaxed_order or strict_order with ef_search=100 restores recall to 100.0% at 100k rows, but latency increases to 40-51ms p50. Meanwhile, exact B-Tree scan takes only 25.98ms p50 with zero recall loss.",
    "partialHnswAdvantage": "Per-domain partial HNSW indexes eliminate cross-domain graph traversal, achieving 1.15ms p50 at 10k rows and 1.59ms p50 at 50k rows, but require maintaining separate indexes per domain."
  }
